    "title": "Setuid or setgid bit set on a file",
    "desc": "A program set the setuid or setgid bit on a file - chmod u+s / g+s, or a numeric mode with the high bit (4xxx / 2xxx / 6xxx). A setuid binary runs with its owner's privileges whoever executes it, so setting the bit (especially owned by root) is a way to plant a privilege-escalation backdoor (MITRE T1548.001). privilege_escalation_attempt catches using sudo/su/pkexec; this catches creating the mechanism.",
